*Experiment - Use date and who in a single command displaying data output on the screen and redirecting who output to a file*

*Command - date; w | cat > http://who.txt*

*Explanation:*
- date - displays the current date and time on the screen
- ; - separates two commands and executes them sequentially
- w - displays information about the currently logged in users
- | - pipe operators, passes the output of w to cat > http://who.txt
- cat > http://who.txt - reads the input received from w and redirects the output into a file (who.txt)

*Procedure -*
1) open the terminal
2) Enter: date ; w | cat > http://who.txt
3) Press enter
4) The date and time are displayed on the screen
5) The output of w is stored in http://who.txt
6) To view the saved output enter: cat http://who.txt

*Result:* The date command output was displayed on the screen, while the output of the w command was successfully redirected and stored into http://who.txt
